    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some help with a big event im planning. we got a lot of dietary restrictions coming in late for this gala we're doing for a law firm (around 500 people) - mostly severe nut allergies and then a bunch of vegans. what's the best way to communicate this to the kitchen so nothing gets missed and how should we label the buffet so people actually see the warnings?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Never underestimate the stakes with nut allergies at a large gathering; immediately draft a separate sealed supply list for the kitchen and assign a dedicated kitchen liaison to double-check every hot line or dish during prep. For the buffet itself, place large, bold \"Allergy Alert\" signage above clearly marked stations for plant-based and nut-free options, ensuring these are easy to see above eye level. Finally, provide each staff member with a small card listing the known restrictions so they can verbally guide guests if the labels aren't immediately noticed.",
